    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "François Rosselet" ; cor:on "2026-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "HOLD lifted: full document compiles via compile_document — one chain of 3 pages, 0.9655/2152 cells; grounds 154 records / 567 promoted / 1194 quarantined. Floor 0.95 chosen as the tighter regression guard. R35 (page-cut key/subtotal degradation) registered with its closure named." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "François Rosselet" ; cor:on "2026-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "Loop N (R35 closed): document-level arithmetic — p2 confirms 21 subtotals with cross-page operands; every record carries its group keys (missing-year-key 0); records 133 / grounded 585 / quarantined 1265; score 0.9655; floor 0.95 re-verified and unchanged." ] ;
    cor:adjudication [ cor:by "composed by Claude Opus 5 (agent), task 5 of the 2026-08-20 arc-denominator loop; the accountable human sign-off is François Rosselet's review and merge of the commit that carries this node" ; cor:on "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
        cor:rationale "SUPERSEDES the 2026-08-02 note above; that note is NOT repaired in place, because this register is an append-only record and a rationale silently rewritten is a rationale nobody can audit. What is superseded: the 2026-08-02 note holds this document on pages 1-2 REGION_TILING_FAILED escalations. Those do not survive at HEAD. Escalation-reason census 2026-08-20 (HEAD 820ab24), § Seam 1: graincorp-stem emits ZERO escalation records, on any page, on any of the nine reasons. § Token accounting for the same run reads 2152 asserted / 77 escalated tokens, and the census states those 77 sit inside asserted regions and mint no record — compile.py:960 accrues escalated_total on a path that makes no escalate_region call — so the page-1/2 reading the 2026-08-02 note describes is now unreproducible from the graph rather than merely repaired. The 2026-08-03 notes stand unchanged and are current: score 0.9655 reproduced in the same census run, clearing cor:scoreFloor 0.95. cor:expectedVerdict stays cor:CompilesAbove; this note retires a stale rationale and does not re-adjudicate the document." ] .

